<article class="env-example" id="0DC5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DC5">Example <span data-tag="0DC5">85.23.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme and let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{C} = X_{spaces, {\acute{e}tale}}$ be the étale site on the category of algebraic spaces étale over $X$, see Properties of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/03G0" data-tag="03G0">66.18.2</a>. Denote $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}$ the structure sheaf, i.e., the sheaf given by the rule $U \mapsto \Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U)$. Denote $\mathcal{A}_ U$ the category of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ U$-modules. Let $\mathcal{B} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ and for $V \in \mathcal{B}$ set $d_ V = 0$ and let $\text{Cov}_ V$ denote the coverings $\{ V_ i \to V\} $ with $V_ i$ affine for all $i$. Then the assumptions (1), (2), (3) are satisfied. See Properties of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/03GA" data-tag="03GA">66.29.2</a> and <a href="/tag/03M1" data-tag="03M1">66.29.7</a> for properties (1) and (2) and the vanishing in (3) follows from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XB" data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</a> and the discussion in Cohomology of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/071Y" data-tag="071Y">69.3</a>. </p>
</article>